title: ARP Spoofing / Cache Poisoning
id: b1cf9de4-d8c4-41bf-9ddc-b27b8da21701
status: experimental
description: Detects ARP spoofing, indicated by multiple IP addresses mapping to a single MAC or rapid gratuitous ARP replies changing a gateway mapping, used for man-in-the-middle interception.
author: Alaris Global
references:
  - https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1557/002/
logsource:
  category: network_connection
detection:
  selection:
    protocol: 'arp'
    arp_anomaly: 'mac_conflict'
  condition: selection
fields:
  - src_ip
  - src_mac
  - dst_ip
falsepositives:
  - Failover/HA appliances sharing MACs
level: high
tags:
  - attack.credential_access
  - attack.t1557.002
